  "aperture_basis": "The source states no clear semi-diameters. Each element is given one clear diameter: the largest of the paraxial marginal-ray and chief-ray envelopes over its own surfaces (marginal ray through the 5 mm exit pupil, chief ray at the stated half field), times a 2 per cent mechanical margin. The envelope is a minimum clear aperture, so every surface of the element passes the axial beam and the chief ray at the full stated field. It is a buildable estimate, not a drawing: no vignetting beyond the stop is modelled and no vignetting figure is claimed.",
  "transcription_notes": "An improvement on the Erfle: better lateral colour, tangential and sagittal fields less widely split, good eye relief, large distortion. The source prints glass 638556 on the third row and marks it as probably a misprint for 638555; the transcription keeps the printed code and states the reading.",
